    "media:imagetext": "aSSoCIaTon OF FLIGHT aTTenDANTS AFLCIO\nApril 26, 1986\nEdith Lauterbach\nsan Francisco, CA\n94131\nDear Edie:\nIt's difficult to know where\nDer to coank vou cor vonn\ntremendous contribution to the flight attendant occupation\nduring the past 42 years.\nit was die to\nyour determination and hard work that the roots\nof our\norganization began\ntake\nwonderful\nability to nurture al\nhold.\nJust as\nyou\nhave the\nFlower from the time it is a\nuntil lt stands tall and proud.\nso have you nurtured\nthe\nfirst flight attendant\ngrow\ninto\nthe present organi-\nzation we call the Association of Elicht Attendantal\nYour list of accomplishments is without equal.\nIn essence,\nwere responsible for beginning\nthe\nYOU\ntransition of our occupation\ncom a cemporaryl\nlow-paying job,\nto a respectable, well-paying\ncareer of\nlifetime.\nWe have recently developed a motto for AFA as we embark into a\nnew era:\nFLIGHT\nATTENDANT\nDIGNITY THROUGH\nFLIGHT ATTENDANT\nI think you will appreciate the full impact of its\nmeaning\nEdie, we will all miss you!\nWith deep appreciation and much affection,\nLinda\nLinda A. Puchala\nPresident",
